# Byte-exact checkout, deliberately.
#
# Several files in this project are sensitive to their exact bytes:
#   - src/*.cpp, src/*.h and scripts/*.ps1 carry a UTF-8 BOM. Without it MSVC may
#     read the Chinese string literals as GBK (the trailing byte of a CJK
#     character swallows the next quote or '%', producing errors that point at
#     unrelated lines), and Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads BOM-less scripts as GBK
#     and fails to parse them outright.
#   - scripts/verify.ps1 asserts on raw byte values (image magic numbers), so
#     silent newline conversion would be a real hazard.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true system-wide, which would rewrite these
# to CRLF on a fresh clone. `-text` disables every line-ending conversion so the
# working tree keeps whatever bytes are in the repository.
* -text
